{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1086518-is-voormas-technically-a-marauder","id":1086518,"title":"Is Voormas technically a Marauder?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-02T01:06:18-07:00","id":1086518,"title":"Is Voormas technically a Marauder?","content":"As the headline suggest I was wondering whether the Grand Harvester could be considered technically a Marauder. While the Euthanatos say that he is barabbi we know that this isn't really the case. Voormas is not a Nephandus, is just mad, and Nephandi are some of his main enemies.<br /> <br /> It'is also said that Voormas suffers the worst kind of jhor the mage world has ever seen, and his morbidity has reached incredible levels: he is obsessed with the thought of his own death, he thinks he is divine, he sees the world rotting around him and so on, basically he fits well in the descriptions of Morbidity 6.<br /> <br /> Also the House of Helekar seemed to me quite the sanity sinkhole: each and every adept he had was a mad rapist-murdered-torturer fanatic, in the first Euthanatos book they said that &quot;the whole house has been infected by his madness&quot;.<br /> <br /> Even more some of his tricks, like killing a Yama King, teleport the whole House of Helekar, and escaping a manhunt made by the whole Council of the Nine Tradition seems more like the wild performance of magic that a marauder could pull.<br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T01:18:03-07:00","id":1086519,"title":"","content":"I can see it. Would be more refreshing than just making him a Nephandus. The Fallen are a dime a dozen. A Morbid Marauder with a god complex is not only more frightening and unpredictable, it reinforces many of the fears the Euthanatoi have about Jhor. THIS is what happens when the death taint grows too strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T01:18:32-07:00","id":1086520,"title":"","content":"That whole barabbi, thing comes from second ed where if you where an evil mage you automatically are labeled nepahadis regardless if you entered a caul or not. Look at the Jade Demon, guys clearly just an infernalist.<br /> <br /> As to your post, there is a difference between mad and Mad. Some could say that the sons of either are a little mad too. Sure the guys a little off his rocker and he has some lofty goals but he isn't a Marauder. <br /> <br /> The poster boy for Jhor tainted yes though. He wants to replace &quot;death&quot; to survive the &quot;end&quot; of the universe, he doesn't think he is &quot;death&quot; noir does he cause reality to reject him like a marauder.<br /> <br /> As for all the stunts he's pulled off, guys an archmage of entropy.<br /> <br /> If you want to see an example of an early stage morbid marauder, look at Herbert West from the Re-Animator films.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 05-02-2017, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T02:35:23-07:00","id":1086528,"title":"","content":"Voormas isn't a Marauder. He's just in a high Paradox Quiet. They're not the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T03:11:09-07:00","id":1086533,"title":"","content":"Voormas isn't a Marauder, NOR is he either an infernalist or a Nephandus. He's Wyrm-tainted the same way Clan Tremere is Wyrm-tainted: <i>death is in him yet still he walks</i>.<br /> <br /> No, Voormas is just evil. You don't need to be a demon-worshipper to be evil. People can do 'evil' all by themselves. That evil is driven by fear, yes, but it's evil nonetheless. Sure, he's got a thousand justifications for what horrifying atrocities he's committed, but Voormas is still <i>evil</i>...!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T04:09:05-07:00","id":1086542,"title":"","content":"I'll echo what the others said.<br /> Voormas isn't a Marauder, nor is he a Nephandus.<br /> <br /> To be a Marauder, you need to actively decide (in whatever delirious state you are in when the forces of Change offer it to you...) to wrap your Paradox around your avatar and become an agent of Change, Chaos and the Wyld. If you decide not to, you forget it ever happened. See Book of Madness 1st ed. for those tasty treats of information, and the M20 anthology story along those lines. Whatever steers them, don't forget that marauders are an actual *faction* in the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> To be a Nephandus, you need to actively decide to fall, walk the Cauls and invert your Avatar to serve personal gain, Descension or the dark masters of various origin.<br /> <br /> In theme with MtA, both those states are voluntary decisions - no matter the circumstances around you, you need to *choose* to become either. Nobody can force you - but they, and whatever state you are in, can make you want to. When it comes to Marauders, the new M20 anthology even has a nice story (&quot;Dabda&quot;) about a sane-ish Hermetic voluntarily entering Marauderdom. A famous Mage of ye olde, Maedea, did the same in order to escape the pressure of Paradox in the modern age. She's a Marauder Oracle now.<br /> <br /> <br /> A mage being evil does not, at all, make him a Nephandus. Nor does a Mage being insane make him a Marauder. Those states can *lead* to that - but they are not the same thing at all. Even if, of course, other Mages just loooove to label evil or insane mages as Nephandi or Marauders to make handling them...less complicated.<br /> <br /> No, Voormas ruthlessy and without regret serves his own vision in his Jhor-drenched view of reality, and he even has bizarrely noble goals - fixing a rotting, deathly world - with the Problem that reaching those goals'd hurt a whole gargantuan truckload of people in the process, and he does not care.<br /> <br /> He's just an evil, reckless A-hole with a ton of sheer metaphysical power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-02-2017, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:21:56-07:00","id":1086617,"title":"","content":"As a twisted metaphor of what means to be mage, Voormas evil it's of his own. He serves no outer forces, no Triat member, no established corporation of Evil. He follows his own brand of evil created by his own egotistic Hubris. He's the &quot;final boss&quot; of his own slice of the evil pie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T09:08:03-07:00","id":1086661,"title":"","content":"I don't really think he works as a Marauder either. I've always felt that there was something very tragic about most Marauders. Even though, on some level, they may have made a choice to break from reality, it wasn't a clear, conscious decision. And while you can have evil, murderous Marauders, others are victims of their circumstances, who still happen to be incredibly dangerous.<br /> <br /> Voormas is arguably insane, and certainly consumed with jhor and morbidity, but that's as a result of his own choices. He gives every indication of being aware of what he's doing and why it's evil, and doesn't care. That's a whole different kettle of fish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}